  "page1": {
    "title": "Telling the Truth, Even When It's Hard",
    "subtitle": "Why honesty takes courage, and how the truth keeps people close.",
    "body": "Mina broke her mom's favorite cup. No one saw it happen. For a moment, she wanted to hide the broken pieces. Telling the truth felt scary. Her heart began to race. But she remembered that lies grow bigger over time. So she walked to her mom and said sorry. Her mom was not angry at all. Instead, she gave Mina a warm hug. \"<mark>Being honest</mark> takes real courage,\" she said. When we tell the truth, people learn to trust us. A lie can hide a problem, but only for a short while. Honesty may feel hard at first. Yet it keeps our hearts light and our friends close. Truth is a gift we give each other.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/04.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A girl tells her mom the truth about a broken cup and receives a warm hug."
  },
